// The memo of successes (docs/syntax.md §4.7, Machine.Memo.cs): a choice whose two
// alternatives read a bracketed nest of the rule itself and are told apart only by the sign
// after it, so that the first alternative reads the nest and is refused, and the second
// reads it again. Read over kinds, where the reader remembers the failures of its recursion,
// `A` remembers its successes too: the probe of both bits at the top of its method, the one
// place its body succeeds through, where the success is written down, and the tape's run of
// cells and the values it keeps. No other snapshot holds any of it.

trivia = { ' '* }

namespace Lexical
{
	trivia = none
	Name = ['a'..'z']+
}

Start : @string = a: A & eof => @(a)
A : @string = b: B => @(b) | c: C => @(c) | n: Lexical.Name => @(n)
B : @string = '(' & a: A & ')' & '+' => @("+" + a)
C : @string = '(' & a: A & ')' & '-' => @("-" + a)

positional parse Start
